,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8270&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=491179&INSPECTION_NN=491179","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"483299","date":"2023-12-05","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8270&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=483299&INSPECTION_NN=483299","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"457421","date":"2023-05-18","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8270&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=457421&INSPECTION_NN=457421","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"444879","date":"2023-01-31","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8270&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=444879&INSPECTION_NN=444879","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"430530","date":"2022-09-12","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":1,"label":"Minor issues","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8270&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=430530&INSPECTION_NN=430530","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":44,"title":"Utensils, equipment & linens: properly stored, dried, & handled","repeat":false,"comment":"4-903.11: (A) clean FOOD-CONTACT surfaces shall be stored: in clean, dry location, not exposed to splash or other contamination, and at least 6 inches above floor. (B) clean EQUIPMENT shall be stored in self-draining position that allows air drying, covered or inverted. (D) Items that are kept in closed PACKAGES may be stored below 6 inches if on dollies, pallets, racks, and skids properly designed. \n\nThe antenna cable for the boom-box radio in the kitchen is observed looping over cleaned/sanitized spatulas on the magnetic rack next to the dish room doorway. This is not a regularly sanitized surface and should not be in contact with food or non-food (magnetic rack) contact surfaces. The cord was removed from the location and the items re-sanitized to correct.","citation":"","citation_text":""}]},{"id":"419123","date":"2022-05-23","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8270&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=419123&INSPECTION_NN=419123","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"408025","date":"2022-01-31","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":1,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"Minor issues","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8270&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=408025&INSPECTION_NN=408025","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":2,"title":"Certified Food Protection Manager (CFPM)","repeat":false,"comment":"2-102.12: (A) The PERSON IN CHARGE shall be a certified FOOD protection manager who has shown proficiency of required information through passing a test that is part of an ACCREDITED PROGRAM. \n\nOn arrival, no CFPM is available in the kitchen. No CFPM arrived during the inspection to correct. Manager at this time is new to the position and in the process of taking the course. Follow up on the next routine inspection.","citation":"","citation_text":""}]},{"id":"384178","date":"2021-04-22","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8270&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=384178&INSPECTION_NN=384178","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"378651","date":"2021-02-04","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8270&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=378651&INSPECTION_NN=378651","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"376362","date":"2020-12-18","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8270&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=376362&INSPECTION_NN=376362","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"371096","date":"2020-09-16","visit":"Spot check","type_raw":"Spot Check","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8270&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=371096&INSPECTION_NN=371096","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"354266","date":"2020-01-21","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8270&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=354266&INSPECTION_NN=354266","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"330942","date":"2019-05-07","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":2,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"Minor issues","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8270&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=330942&INSPECTION_NN=330942","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":8,"title":"Hands clean and properly washed","repeat":false,"comment":"","citation":"2-301.12","citation_text":"2-301.12 (C) (P) (C) To avoid recontaminating their hands or surrogate prosthetic devices, FOOD EMPLOYEES may use disposable paper towels or similar clean barriers when touching surfaces such as manually operated faucet handles on a HAND WASHING SINK.\nAn employee was observed turning of the faucet without a clean barrier after washing their hands. Another was observed using a paper towel to urn off the faucet then use that same towel to dry off their hands. Hand washing procedures were discussed with the PIC and they were instructed to ensure education of the staff."},{"item":23,"title":"Proper date marking and disposition","repeat":false,"comment":"","citation":"3-501.17","citation_text":"3-501.17 (A) (Pf) Refrigerated, READY-TO-EAT, TIME/TEMPERATURE CONTROL FOR SAFETY FOOD prepared and held in a FOOD ESTABLISHMENT for more than 24 hours shall be clearly marked to indicate the date or day by which the FOOD shall be consumed on the PREMISES, sold, or discarded at a maximum of 7 days. The day of preparation shall be counted as Day 1.\nCottage cheese was observed open and with a date mark of 4/29. Today is day 8 of the 7 days. Date marking rules were discussed and the container was discarded during the inspection."}]},{"id":"322042","date":"2019-02-04","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8270&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=322042&INSPECTION_NN=322042","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"273990","date":"2018-05-01","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8270&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=273990&INSPECTION_NN=273990","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"266934","date":"2018-01-29","vis